  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1209 AM CDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\nNot many changes to the longer term forecast, with the hot and dry\nconditions continuing into next week and likely into next weekend.\nUpper level ridge axis shifts to the southeast US but remains\nstrong enough to keep any systems from approaching from the\nsouthwest US. Temperatures will remain above normal, partly\nbecause of the ongoing very dry conditions and the lack of much\nin the way of soil moisture. This means the hottest temperatures\nwill remain across the areas that have been the driest, mainly the\nBig Country, where readings will continue to climb above the 100\ndegree mark. Farther south, a little more recent rainfall on\nThursday, plus a little more farther away from the ridge axis,\nmeans highs will remain in the mid/upper 90s across the Hill\nCountry and Edwards Plateau.",
